# Round 14 reconciliation: implementers A and B against the official SHAP comparison outputs

Names: SHAP = `D:\treeroute\analysis\shap_v1`; V = `SHAP\verify_v1`; "official" = the outputs of
`SHAP\scripts\compare_shap.py` in `SHAP\out\<p>\lead_0\compare\`. Written 2026-11-16 by the reconciler. Everything
written in this round by the reconciler is in `V\reconcile\` (list at the end); no other file was changed.

## In short

- **Every number the official files hold agrees with A and with B** (within 1e-9; the largest difference among the
  matched numbers is 1.6e-15), except where the protocol leaves a choice open and the two implementers or
  compare_shap chose differently. A and B agree with each other on every number except three open choices.
- **Two places where compare_shap.py does not do what the protocol's words say** (findings for the owner; no file
  was changed):
  1. **Fire's main-text row has no treeroute top 3 and no treeroute own-history share.** Section 8 asks for both, and
     the brief says they "still have values" for fire. A and B agree on them: top 3 hist_mean, spei, tslf_months;
     own-history share 0.136 [0.108, 0.165]. The full-sample values can be found in the official importance and
     family files, but the interval is in no official file.
  2. **The sign agreement has no interval.** Section 8 says every statistic is recomputed on the draws. compare_shap
     computes the sign agreement on the full sample only, and its file says "0 finite replicates" although no draw was
     tried. A and B computed the intervals and agree. The values themselves are right.
- **B1:** finished on defo, fire, pm25 and ndvi; not defined on coral. Defo's identity check gives exactly 0 at both
  levels, with the same rows, players and variables (A, B and the reconciler's own recomputation). A and B agree on
  every fire, pm25 and ndvi B1 number except one open choice (B adds a feature-level family distance). Their nonzero
  counts equal each B1 `meta.json`. No number of items 1-8 depends on B1.
- Verdict: **every mismatch is explained.** 72,974 keys mismatch, almost all because the official files simply do
  not hold a number that A and B computed (mostly intervals of the per-model importances, a format choice).

