and B's `results.json` under `b1`.

**What the reconciliation changes for B1.** Section 10 says the B1 numbers make compare_shap's choice wherever
section 8 leaves one open. Two such choices differ from what A and B did: (a) counts have no interval in compare_shap,
so the B1 counts should be reported without intervals (values unchanged); (b) compare_shap has no feature-level family
distance, so B's B1 value is dropped (A has none). Both are changes of presentation; no B1 number has to be
recomputed. The B1 importances, shares, signed means, family shares, own-history share and pair statistics keep their
intervals, because section 10 asks for them in so many words ("every number above recomputed on each draw;
percentile 95% intervals ... none for the top-k lists").

**`per_lead.json`'s `models` lists `treeroute_B1` in no problem** (checked in the official files; A and B say the
same).

**No number of items 1-8 depends on B1:**

- Official files: `compare_shap.py` reads only folders named `treeroute` or `rival_*` (line 88); `per_lead.json`'s
  `models` never holds `treeroute_B1`; every comparison was finished before the first B1 run started (2026-11-15
  23:06:16): coral 2026-11-13 00:06, fire 2026-11-14 04:47, pm25 04:47, defo 14:35, ndvi 2026-11-15 19:11 (the done
  records' `finished` times and the files' modification times agree). The official treeroute importances equal A's
  main-run values (largest difference 2.8e-17) and differ from the B1 run's (up to 0.013 in I on fire, 0.20 on pm25,
  0.046 on ndvi). On defo the B1 run equals the main run exactly, so it could not change a number either.
- A's code: `a10_items1_8.py` and `a05_global_rule.py` open only the pieces of `per_lead.json`'s `models` (a10 stops
  if `treeroute_B1` is among them); its record of opened files (`V\A\work\opened_items_<p>.json`) names no B1 file.
  Only `a20_b1.py` opens `treeroute_B1\`.
- B's code: `b_compare.py` and `b_global_index.py` open only the pieces of `models` (b_compare asserts that
  `treeroute_B1` is not among them). Only `b_b1.py` and `b_crosscheck_b1.py` open `treeroute_B1\`.

